      "_curated_match": false,
      "bio_summary": {
        "value": "Jennifer Capps Balkcom (born 1978 or 1979) is an American politician serving as a member of the North Carolina House of Representatives for the 117th district since 2023. [ 1 ] [ 2 ] She is the Republican nominee for North Carolina's 11th congressional district in 2026 . Early life and education [ edit ] Balkcom was born in 1978 or 1979. [ 3 ] She graduated from Blue Ridge Community College with an associate degree in applied science and business administration. [ 4 ] Career [ edit ] Early career [ edit ] Balkcom has worked as a financial industry since 1998 [ 5 ] and works as a mortgage loan officer for ALCOVA as of August 2026. [ 6 ] Before being elected to the North Carolina House of Representatives, she was active in many local nonprofits, was a member of the Henderson County planning board, and served on the board of the AdventHealth Foundation . [ 4 ] ",
